0..79 Comment "/// A transport whose motive starts at another point than its moved path prints"
80..107 Comment "/// as the transport it is."
108..111 Comment "///"
112..188 Comment "/// A transport along `r` of `Path.here(f)`, under a motive `Path(C, l, c)`,"
189..263 Comment "/// is the composite `Path.step(Path.here(f), r)` exactly when `l` is `f`."
264..341 Comment "/// Reading that composite back takes the motive\'s start from `Path.here(f)`."
342..415 Comment "/// A motive that starts at `Path.step(f, Path.here(z))` is another type,"
416..455 Comment "/// which the composite does not spell."
456..459 Comment "///"
460..537 Comment "/// The printer writes a transport as a composite only where the moved path\'s"
538..607 Comment "/// start is the motive\'s. Otherwise it writes the transport in full."
608..611 Comment "///"
612..683 Comment "/// - see: #4218 — the printer wrote both transports as one composite"
684..754 Comment "/// - see: #754 — a returned composite of paths is written as a step"
756..831 Comment "/// Motives whose fixed starts differ by the right unit of a variable path."
